  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Statement I: Leaching of gold with cyanide ion in absence of air / <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> leads to cyano complex of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Au</mi></math>(III).</p><p>Statement II: Zinc is oxidized during the displacement reaction carried out for gold extraction.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below.</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Both Statement 1 and statement 2&nbsp; are correct",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Both Statement 1 and statement 2&nbsp;are incorrect",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Statement 1 is correct&nbsp;but statement 2 is incorrect",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Statement 1 is&nbsp;incorrect&nbsp;but statement 2 is correct",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Au</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><msup><mi>CN</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Au</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>The oxidation state of gold in the complex is +1.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Au</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>Zn</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Au</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Zn</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>The oxidation state of zinc&nbsp;in the complex is +2.</p><p>Oxidation state of Zn in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Zn</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;+2.</p><p>As, Oxidation state of zinc is converted from zero(elemental state) to +2.It&nbsp; is undergoing oxidation.</p><p>Hence,Statement 1 is&nbsp;incorrect&nbsp;but statement 2 is correct</p>"
